  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Widely scattered and isolated showers possible \nSaturday and Sunday, though primarily dry weather will dominate \nthrough Labor Day.\n\nMid-level trough centered over New England today, will gradually \nexit east into the north Atlantic through the holiday weekend, \nplacing the eastern Great Lakes beneath northwest flow. While the \ntrough exits east a few disturbances will dive southeast across the \nregion. Meanwhile, at the surface, high pressure over the upper \nGreat Lakes this morning will slide southeast across the eastern \nGreat Lakes towards the mid-Atlantic by Monday.\n\nOverall, mainly dry weather will prevail throughout this holiday \nweekend, however with each shortwave disturbance passage a few \nwidely scattered and isolated showers will be possible.\n\nOtherwise, expect near-average to slightly below average \ntemperatures through the weekend. Lingering moisture, cool \ntemperatures, and calm winds will yield patchy river valley fog \nacross the Finger Lakes, east of Lake Ontario and across the western \nSouthern Tier every night.",
